// The committed half of the demo's configuration.
//
// It exists so a clean clone builds. `Config.xcconfig` holds the real ingest key and is
// gitignored, which means it is absent on a fresh checkout — and xcodegen refuses to generate a
// project whose config file is missing. So the project points at this file, which is always here,
// and this file pulls the other one in optionally: `#include?` is silent when the target is not
// there. The defaults below are what a clone therefore builds with, and a blank key is the
// signal the app reads to initialise nothing at all.
//
// Copy `Config.example.xcconfig` to `Config.xcconfig` to fill them in.

// A url cannot be written literally in an xcconfig: `//` starts a comment, so
// `http://localhost:8080` would silently set the endpoint to `http:`. The slashes come from a
// variable instead, which is the usual way round it.
SLASH = /

ANALYTICS_API_KEY =
ANALYTICS_ENDPOINT = http:$(SLASH)$(SLASH)localhost:8080

#include? "Config.xcconfig"
